case Statements
case statements allow for selecting one of several choices
case word in
pattern) commands ;;
pattern) commands ;;
...
esac
compares word to each of the patterns in turn and executes the commands for the first match found
Efficient way to check arguments
case $# in
0)	echo "Usage: $0 args..." ; exit 1 ;;
1)  arg1=$1; arg2="default" ;;
*)  arg1=$1; arg2=$2 ;;
esac
